1797, oil on canvas. By Thomas Lawrence (1769-1833). Courtesy of the Charles Darwin Foundation. From the private collection of Mrs. Margaret Darwin, granddaughter of Charles Darwin. First exhibited in the Darwin Museum, Oxford; It is now preserved in the St Andrews University Library.
The world's greatest expert, Daniel George Brown (1773–1848), worked as an entomologist at the London Zoo. Charles died on the voyage that brought Darwin to England, leaving Darwin and his uncle John his entire botanical collection, including many specimens of flies and butterflies. Brauey's personal paper diary is now held at the Darwin Museum, Oxford.
